## Rust structure

### Guideline

- Keep `src/main.rs` or `src/bin/*.rs` thin: parse arguments, build the dependency graph, run.
- Give each concept its own module under `src/`, re-exported from `lib.rs`.
- Split a multi-purpose binary into workspace crates along actor lines (a domain crate, an application crate, adapter crates), never one crate that several teams edit for unrelated reasons.
- Keep unit tests beside their code in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`; keep integration tests of the public API under `tests/`.
<!-- Project-specific / Rust-Guideline -->

### Layout

```
├── assets/             # repository assets (images, logos, etc)
├── benches/            # benchmarks (cargo bench)
├── crates/             # workspace member crates (workspace projects)
├── docs/               # design and user documents
├── examples/           # examples for applications and/or public libraries (cargo run --example <name>)
├── scripts/            # build/install/analysis scripts
├── src/                # library/binary source (lib.rs, main.rs, bin/*.rs)
├── tests/              # integration tests of the public API
├── Cargo.lock          # dependency lockfile (committed for binaries)
├── Cargo.toml          # package manifest / workspace definition
├── Dockerfile          # container build definition
├── Makefile            # build/test/lint task automation (optional)
├── clippy.toml         # Clippy lint configuration (optional)
├── deny.toml           # cargo-deny policy: licenses, advisories, banned crates (optional)
├── rust-toolchain.toml # pinned Rust toolchain (optional)
<!-- Project-specific / Rust-Layout -->
```

### Layer Dependencies

Notes for declaring layers in the `Layer Dependencies` section of `.attunic/context.md`; adjust them to the project before declaring.

- `crates/cli` (or `src/main.rs` in a single-crate project) is the outermost layer and the composition root: the only place that names a concrete adapter type; it may depend on everything, and nothing depends on it.
- Layers are workspace crates; one suggestion, innermost first:

| Layer | Typical path | Depends on | Must never contain |
|-------|--------------|------------|--------------------|
| domain | crates/domain | itself | HTTP client, database driver, async runtime |
| application | crates/application | domain | database access, HTTP handlers |
| adapters | crates/adapters/\* | application (its ports), domain | business rules |
| main | crates/cli | application, adapters, domain | business rules |

- Declare ports as traits in the domain or application crate; adapter crates implement them, and path dependencies point outward-to-inward only.
- Check by hand: `cargo tree` (or reading each crate's `Cargo.toml`) must never show an inner crate depending on an outer one.
